D:\Downloads\Final Year Project\ideaspark_run\world-model-quantization\terminal_logs\phase2_3_coherence.stderr.log:1151:Freeze a public DreamerV3- or TD-MPC2-style action-conditioned latent world model at FP16 (an inferred pilot anchor, not a prior claim or a new backbone), add no foundation-model pretraining, and use the existing uniform-affine PyTorch torch.ao.quantization path as the numerical weight/activation PTQ operator. Let G be the deterministic set of every eligible Linear or Conv weight tensor and its activation output reached by the planner's scoring forward path; optimizer state and planner-only code are not quantized, and each g has a measured peak-byte cost m_g(b). From named DeepMind Control Suite (DMC) visual continuous-control tasks, collect disjoint self-built calibration and evaluation streams, with each record r storing the model-internal latent z_t, a planner-generated candidate set U_t, and its horizon, update schedule, receding-horizon convention, and tie rule. Use the pre-registered grid H={floor(H_native/2), H_native, min(2H_native,H_episode)}, N={max(1,floor(N_native/2)), N_native, 2N_native}, M={max(1,floor(M0/4)), max(1,floor(M0/2)), M0}, S={s_native, random shooting, CEM}, E={e_native, one-step}, and T={stable-index, seeded-random}, removing duplicate cells; M0 is the largest per-cell trajectory count fitting the fixed A100 pilot envelope, and grid-cell weights omega_c default to 1/|C| unless deployment frequencies are preregistered. For each g and allowed bit pair b in B={(FP16,FP16), W8A8, W8A4, W4A8, W4A4}, quantize only g with the same observer/calibration data, keep every other site FP16, rerun the identical candidate set under cell c, and define d_g,c(r;b) as the normalized pairwise candidate-order disagreement from FP16 with ties resolved by tau. The central object is the rollout-ranking influence profile I_g,c(b)=average_r in D_c of d_g,c(r;b) and I_g(b)=sum_c omega_c I_g,c(b), a dimensionless counterfactual estimand of how much site g changes planner ordering over the observed rollout regime; fixed-size per-cell accumulators compute this mean exactly for the stated site-only estimand rather than approximating an unchosen Shapley value. The heterogeneous companion partitions sites by their full vector (I_g,c(b)) across cells and chooses b_g by minimizing sum_g omega_g I_g(b_g) subject to sum_g m_g(b_g) <= M_mem, where omega_g defaults to 1/|G| and M_mem is swept over the Pareto range from an FP16-feasible target to the lowest supported bit mix. The resulting all-sites assignment is evaluated end-to-end on disjoint episodes for every grid cell and memory target, reporting rank agreement, first-action agreement, closed-loop return or success, peak memory, and control frequency; the influence profile is therefore an empirical allocation signal rather than a claim of global optimality. A matched intervention keeps candidate pools, start states, bit histogram, memory target, planner schedule, receding-horizon convention, and tie rule fixed while randomizing the mapping from I_g to bit pairs, so any downstream advantage must come from the computed decision influence rather than bit count or local tensor error. The evidence boundary is explicit: arxiv:2602.02110v1 is connector-verified host_recall with fulltext H/html_arxiv, arxiv:2608.24855v1 is arxiv-retrieved with fulltext T3/html_arxiv, and arxiv:2607.28405v1 is connector-verified host_recall but has no fulltext cache entry in this run and is used only as an abstract-only adjacent comparison; none is introduced as the backbone.
