D:\Downloads\Final Year Project\ideaspark_run\world-model-quantization\terminal_logs\phase2_3_coherence.stderr.log:2398:+      "value": "Freeze a public DreamerV3- or TD-MPC2-style action-conditioned latent world model at FP16 (an inferred pilot anchor, not a prior claim or a new backbone), add no foundation-model pretraining, and use the existing uniform-affine PyTorch torch.ao.quantization path as the numerical weight/activation PTQ operator; this numerical path is an emulation boundary and is not evidence that an A100 has a deployable W4A4 kernel. Let G be the deterministic union, over every declared grid cell, of every eligible Linear or Conv weight tensor W_g and its activation output A_g reached by the planner's scoring forward path; optimizer state and planner-only code are not quantized, each g has a measured per-site storage record m_g(b), and require |G| >= 1. From named DeepMind Control Suite (DMC) visual continuous-control tasks, collect disjoint self-built calibration and evaluation streams, with each record r storing the complete planner replay state q_t (including z_t and any recurrent/history/cache/normalization/RNG state needed to replay the scoring path), a planner-generated candidate set U_t, and its horizon, update schedule, receding-horizon convention, and tie rule. Use the pre-registered grid H={max(1,floor(H_native/2)), H_native, min(2H_native,H_episode)}, N={max(1,floor(N_native/2)), N_native, 2N_native}, M={max(1,floor(M0/4)), max(1,floor(M0/2)), M0}, S={s_native, random shooting, CEM}, E={e_native, one-step}, and T={stable-index, seeded-random}, removing duplicate cells; define M0 as the minimum, over the non-M base cells, of the largest positive per-cell trajectory count fitting the fixed A100 pilot envelope, and let grid-cell weights omega_c default to 1/|C| unless deployment frequencies are preregistered. Let B={(FP16,FP16), W8A8, W8A4, W4A8, W4A4} be the analysis bit-pair set, and let B_deploy be the subset with a measured backend-supported weight/activation implementation; fake-quant-only pairs may be profiled numerically but cannot enter deployment Pareto curves or the lowest supported deployment target. For each g and b in B, quantize only g with the same observer/calibration data, keep every other site FP16, rerun the identical candidate set under cell c, and define d_g,c(r;b) as the normalized pairwise candidate-order disagreement from FP16 using the explicit tie rule below. The central object is the rollout-ranking influence profile I_g,c(b)=average_r in D_c of d_g,c(r;b) and I_g(b)=sum_c omega_c I_g,c(b), a dimensionless counterfactual estimand of how much site g changes planner ordering over the observed rollout regime; finite accumulators compute the stated finite-sample estimator, subject to ordinary numerical rounding, rather than approximating an unchosen Shapley value. The heterogeneous companion retains each full profile vector P_g=(I_g,c(b)) across cells as its heterogeneity representation (no unbound clustering rule) and chooses b_g by minimizing sum_g omega_g I_g(b_g) subject to the system-level PeakBytes(b_1,...,b_|G|) <= M_mem, where PeakBytes is measured on the materialized end-to-end graph and includes resident weights, activation lifetimes and shared tensors, scales/zero-points, weight copies, and backend workspace; m_g(b) remains a diagnostic per-site record, not a quantity to sum as though sites were disjoint. The resulting all-sites assignment is evaluated end-to-end on disjoint episodes for every feasible grid cell and memory target, reporting rank agreement, first-action agreement, closed-loop return or success, peak memory, and control frequency; the influence profile is therefore an empirical allocation signal rather than a claim of global optimality. A matched intervention keeps candidate pools, start states, bit histogram, exact measured PeakBytes, memory target, planner schedule, receding horizon convention, and tie rule fixed while sampling only non-identity assignments with the same bit-pair histogram and exact measured PeakBytes; if no such assignment exists, the negative control is recorded as unavailable. This control tests attribution under matched conditions but does not prove causality or guarantee a downstream gain. The evidence boundary is explicit: arxiv:2602.02110v1 is connector-verified host_recall with fulltext H/html_arxiv, arxiv:2608.24855v1 is arxiv-retrieved with fulltext T3/html_arxiv, and arxiv:2607.28405v1 is connector-verified host_recall but has no fulltext cache entry in this run and is used only as an abstract-only adjacent comparison; none is introduced as the backbone.",
